From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Corrales <deathcamel58@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:45:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: add the inMusic AZ01 fan controller

The motorized AZ01 players (Denon DJ SC5000M and SC6000M) have fans that
the SoC does not drive. A microcontroller on UART1 runs them; the host
sets a level and the microcontroller reports back:

  host -> MCU   00 LL            fan level, 0..255
  MCU -> host   01 AH AL BH BL   two big-endian 16-bit fan readings

at 115200 baud, 8N1, without flow control. The device trees describe it
as a serdev child of the UART, compatible "inmusic,az01-fan", with
#cooling-cells and cooling maps from 75 to 100 C on both thermal zones.
Without a driver the fans are never commanded.

Register the level as a thermal cooling device (max state 255, as the
cooling maps expect) and the two readings as hwmon fan1_input and
fan2_input, unscaled. The protocol was read out of the vendor kernel's
driver; this is a separate implementation of it. Add the binding and
the inmusic vendor prefix.

UNTESTED ON HARDWARE: built with W=1 and checked with checkpatch, and the
frame parser was exercised on a host. Whether the readings are RPM, and
how the MCU behaves before the first level is sent, is unconfirmed.

Upstream-Status: Pending [untested on hardware]
